<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  cyclonedds-container.xml — MANUAL, OPT-IN loopback DDS transport fallback.

  ⛔ NOT wired into scripts/cloud-bootstrap.sh — WE RELY ON CYCLONEDDS DEFAULTS.
    Measured on two cloud containers (2026-09-16): default discovery picks a
    multicast-capable NIC (eth0, flags 0x1003) and works cross-process — verified by a
    2167-sample ddsmonitor capture and the ClusterRunner DDS integration suites. An earlier
    version of the bootstrap exported CYCLONEDDS_URI pointing here to pin loopback, but `lo`
    ships WITHOUT the MULTICAST flag on at least one container and enabling it needs
    CAP_NET_ADMIN (denied there), so the pin only fell back to default anyway. Net benefit
    over defaults: zero. This file is kept ONLY as a manual escape hatch.

  WHEN TO USE IT (rare)
    Only if a future container's default discovery genuinely fails (e.g. no multicast-capable
    NIC at all). Then, after enabling lo multicast (`ip link set dev lo multicast on`, needs
    CAP_NET_ADMIN), export it for the cluster AND ddsmonitor:
      export CYCLONEDDS_URI="file://$PWD/config/cyclonedds-container.xml"
    It pins every process to loopback+multicast, self-contained (no external NIC).

  IT IS TRANSPORT-ONLY, ON PURPOSE
    - <Domain Id="any"> => applies to EVERY domain, including the integration tests' 100-500
      range (DistributedScenarioSaveTests base 271, NetworkGatewayIntegrationTests base 230,
      CgfHarness base 200). Test isolation is by DomainId, which this does not touch.
    - It sets NO discovery peer list, NO QoS, NO domain-0 pinning — so it changes HOW packets
      travel, never WHO talks to WHOM. Domains stay isolated.

  SCOPE / CAVEAT
    lo-only means processes talk over loopback ONLY — correct for a single container, wrong
    for genuine cross-container DDS. This file is a container-debugging convenience, not a
    deployment config. Override per-command with `env -u CYCLONEDDS_URI ...` (e.g. to let
    ddsmonitor use default discovery), or point CYCLONEDDS_URI elsewhere.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config"
            xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
            xsi:schemaLocation="https://cdds.io/config https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eclipse-cyclonedds/cyclonedds/master/etc/cyclonedds.xsd">
  <Domain Id="any">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface name="lo" multicast="true"/>
      </Interfaces>
      <AllowMulticast>true</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
